<title>GREECE: MACEDONIA THRACE BANK CUTS DEPO, LOAN RATES.</title>
<headline>MACEDONIA THRACE BANK CUTS DEPO, LOAN RATES.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Macedonia Thrace Bank </p>
<p>will cut its lending and deposit rates effective May 1, it said</p>
<p>on Friday.</p>
<p>The bank will offer the following rate structure:</p>
<p>LENDING RATES</p>
<p>    ** Base lending rate for working capital    20.0 percent</p>
<p>** Base lending rate for fixed asset loans  15.75</p>
<p>    ** Consumer loans				   19.50</p>
<p>    ** Personal loans				   21.25</p>
<p>    ** Auto loans					 18.00</p>
<p>    ** Mortgages					  14.00</p>
<p>DEPOSIT RATES</p>
<p>    ** Savings deposit				  9.0-9.5 percent</p>
<p>** Time deposits</p>
<p>	 Three, six months				9.75</p>
<p>	 Nine, 12 months				  9.50</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
